{"content":[{"c":["TALITHA CUMI*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Aramaic words spoken by Jesus and retained by Mark in his Gospel (",{"href":"?bref=Mark.5.41","r":"Mark.5.41","rawR":"Mark.5.41","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.5.41","value":"Mark.5.41"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mk 5:41"},"). Jairus, a synagogue official in the Galilean region, called on Jesus to heal his sick daughter; however, she died before Jesus arrived. Coming to the girl, Jesus took her hand and said, ",{"c":["“Talitha cumi,”"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," meaning “Little girl, arise.” ",{"c":["“Talitha”"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," is a term of affection meaning “lamb” or “youth.” ",{"c":["“Cumi”"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," is a command to rise up, translated by Mark as “I say to you, arise!”"],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["In his Gospel, Mark includes other Aramaic phrases attributed to Jesus (",{"href":"?bref=Mark.3.17","r":"Mark.3.17","rawR":"Mark.3.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.3.17","value":"Mark.3.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mk 3:17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.5.41","r":"Mark.5.41","rawR":"Mark.5.41","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.5.41","value":"Mark.5.41"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:41"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.7.11,34","r":"Mark.7.11,34","rawR":"Mark.7.11,34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.7.11,34","value":"Mark.7.11,34"}],"t":"ref","v":"7:11, 34"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.11.9-10","r":"Mark.11.9-10","rawR":"Mark.11.9-10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.11.9-10","value":"Mark.11.9-10"}],"t":"ref","v":"11:9-10"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.14.36","r":"Mark.14.36","rawR":"Mark.14.36","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.14.36","value":"Mark.14.36"}],"t":"ref","v":"14:36"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.15.22,34","r":"Mark.15.22,34","rawR":"Mark.15.22,34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.15.22,34","value":"Mark.15.22,34"}],"t":"ref","v":"15:22, 34"},"). Matthew retains only two Aramaic phrases (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.27.33,46","r":"Matt.27.33,46","rawR":"Matt.27.33,46","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.27.33,46","value":"Matt.27.33,46"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 27:33, 46"},"), and Luke keeps none."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"TalithaCumi","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Mk 5:41","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Mark.5.41","rawQueryValue":"Mark.5.41","sourceRefExact":"Mark.5.41"},{"anchorText":"Mk 3:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Mark.3.17","rawQueryValue":"Mark.3.17","sourceRefExact":"Mark.3.17"},{"anchorText":"5:41","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Mark.5.41","rawQueryValue":"Mark.5.41","sourceRefExact":"Mark.5.41"},{"anchorText":"7:11, 34","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Mark.7.11,34","rawQueryValue":"Mark.7.11,34","sourceRefExact":"Mark.7.11,34"},{"anchorText":"11:9-10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Mark.11.9-10","rawQueryValue":"Mark.11.9-10","sourceRefExact":"Mark.11.9-10"},{"anchorText":"14:36","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Mark.14.36","rawQueryValue":"Mark.14.36","sourceRefExact":"Mark.14.36"},{"anchorText":"15:22, 34","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Mark.15.22,34","rawQueryValue":"Mark.15.22,34","sourceRefExact":"Mark.15.22,34"},{"anchorText":"Mt 27:33, 46","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.27.33,46","rawQueryValue":"Matt.27.33,46","sourceRefExact":"Matt.27.33,46"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"94f2a8081f81886260729481386805da2e38281ce719e23391855db702d56c6a","sourceItemName":"TalithaCumi","sourceItemOrder":34,"sourceMember":"Articles/T.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"TalithaCumi"